 -4star-theater-oct-1522/\nLocation: san francisco\nCategories: community\n
 Source: funcheap/san-francisco\n\nForget the guilt trip\, the Green Film F
 estival of San Francisco\, the mischievous\, tree-hugging cousin of the 29
  year old SF IndieFest\, returns Oct 15-22\, 2026 to prove that saving the
  planet doesn’t have to feel like homework. We’ve ditched the doom-and
 -gloom documentaries that make you want to crawl under a (sustainably sour
 ced) blanket and never come out. Tickets for live shows are $15.90. Festiv
 al pass is $97.96 MOVIES FOR ALL : With proof of an EBT/SNAP card\, folks 
 are eligible for $5 movie tickets at the Green Film Festival. Tickets are 
 redeemable online or at the box office. For ordering live shows online\, p
 lease be prepared to show your EBT card when checking in at the box office
 . To order tickets to virtual presentations email a photo of yourself hold
 ing your card to info@sfindie.com to unlock your $5 tickets to virtual sho
 ws. The discount code to use when checking out at the box office is “ mo
 viesforall .” Limit one ticket per show per cardholder. The line-up this
  year pairs sharp environmental storytelling with wit\, weirdness\, and un
 apologetic irreverence. And yes\, our Eco-Horror midnight movie is back! W
 hether you’re an eco-curious cinephile or a die-hard activist\, come
LOCATION:san francisco
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/2026-green-film-festival-san-francisco-4star-t
 heater-oct-1522/
